		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Battle Checkers for iPhone/iPod Touch]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=13293#p13293"><![CDATA[
Game we used to play when we were kids - Chapaev (<a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chapayev_%28game%29" class="postlink">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chapayev_(game)</a>.  After getting tired of thinking (playing real checkers), lined up the pegs, flexed our fingers, and start flicking/shooting pegs trying to knock each others pegs off the board. <br><br>The core of the game is a slightly optimized Bullet (as part of Oolong Engine by Wolfgang Engel).  Kudos to Erwin! Every single place that needed to be modified was already either a virtual function, or otherwise "hookable". <br><br>In addition to classic gameplay, over 30 different layouts were added.<br><br>I have the same feeling about Bullet as I had about SQLite (long before it's current dominating position on all platforms).<br><br>Anyways, the game is available from iTunes <a href="http://itunes.apple.com/WebObjects/MZStore.woa/wa/viewSoftware?id=310658947&amp;mt=8" class="postlink">http://itunes.apple.com/WebObjects/MZSt ... 58947&amp;mt=8</a><br>Will update the topic with a link to free version when it gets approved.<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=267" class="postimage" alt="Another screenshot" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><br /><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=266" class="postimage" alt="Battle Checkers Screenshot" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4999">dns</a> — Mon Apr 13, 2009 5:37 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
